.uv/

# --- hatch-vcs generated ---
src/chainlens/_version.py

# --- Docs build ---
book/

# --- Notebooks ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Front-end build ---
# The app's source and its generated wire schema are committed; its dependency tree, its
# intermediate build output and its coverage are not. The *finished* bundle is committed too,
# and it lives inside the package (`src/chainlens/ui/static/`) because that is what ships in
# the wheel. `make ui` builds it; CI rebuilds it and fails on a diff, so a stale bundle cannot
# be shipped silently.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/coverage/
# Not prefixed with `web/`, because a tool run from the repository root rather than from `web/`
# creates exactly this directory here — a cache, not a dependency tree — and it would otherwise
# be staged by the next `git add -A`.
node_modules/
.vite/

# --- Editors / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Secrets: never commit provider keys ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key

# --- Case study corpus ---
# Full post text and screenshots stay out of the repository: what is committed is
# a redacted URL, a content hash and a short quote. See case-study/README.md.
# results/ is deliberately NOT ignored — the generated report is the deliverable.
case-study/corpus/

# --- Case study inbox ---
# Where posts are dropped for `make ingest` to digest. Both the drops and where they
# end up are local; only the manifest entry is committed.
case-study/inbox/
